description: P2PFlow MVP cross-repository architecture and service boundaries.
globs:
alwaysApply: false
---

# architecture.mdc

```yaml
architecture:
  summary: P2PFlow is a three-sided USDC-to-INR/UPI peer marketplace on an EIP-2535 Diamond. Users create BUY or SELL orders, approved merchants fulfill fiat legs, and authenticated operators manage merchants, disputes, prices, and emergency controls. The MVP uses three React clients, a Diamond contract, one Goldsky subgraph read model, and exactly one modular executor service for pricing, matching, event recovery, transactions, sessions, and operations.

  style: multi-repository platform with one modular executor deployable

  layers:
    - name: http
      paths:
        - ../p2pflow-user-ui/src/App.jsx
        - ../p2pflow-merchant-ui/src/App.jsx
        - ../p2pflow-admin-ui/src/App.jsx
        - ../p2pflow-executor/src/http
    - name: business
      paths:
        - contracts/facets
        - contracts/libraries
        - ../p2pflow-executor/src/modules/pricing
        - ../p2pflow-executor/src/modules/matching
        - ../p2pflow-executor/src/modules/sessions
        - ../p2pflow-executor/src/modules/orders
        - ../p2pflow-user-ui/src/hooks
        - ../p2pflow-merchant-ui/src/hooks
        - ../p2pflow-admin-ui/src/hooks
    - name: infrastructure
      paths:
        - contracts/shared
        - scripts
        - ../p2pflow-subgraph/src
        - ../p2pflow-executor/src/chain
        - ../p2pflow-executor/src/db
        - ../p2pflow-executor/src/queue
        - ../p2pflow-executor/src/providers
        - ../p2pflow-user-ui/src/thirdweb
        - ../p2pflow-merchant-ui/src/thirdweb
        - ../p2pflow-admin-ui/src/thirdweb

  boundaries:
    - The Diamond is authoritative for custody, order transitions, roles, pause state, merchant/channel eligibility, and current liquidity guardrails.
    - The executor may discover and rank from indexed data but must submit exact candidates for independent contract revalidation.
    - The subgraph is an eventually consistent query projection and must never authorize a financial action.
    - Browser applications contain only public configuration and never privileged credentials or authoritative payment data.
    - All executor capabilities run as modules in one process and one deployment artifact; modules communicate through typed interfaces and a shared PostgreSQL transaction boundary.
    - P2P.me repositories are reference-only and cannot be imported as runtime dependencies.

  integrations:
    - Base Sepolia JSON-RPC and WebSocket providers
    - Circle Base Sepolia USDC at 0x036CbD53842c5426634e7929541eC2318f3dCF7e
    - Thirdweb embedded and external wallets
    - Goldsky hosted subgraph
    - PostgreSQL durable jobs, cursors, sessions, reservations, and audit records
    - multiple independent market and INR FX price providers
    - operator health metrics and alerts

  auth:
    userFacingPattern: wallet auto-connect plus nonce/signature backend session in Secure HttpOnly cookie
    partnerPattern: server-verified wallet roles with Diamond role revalidation for privileged actions
    configPaths:
      - ../p2pflow-user-ui/src/components/Auth
      - ../p2pflow-merchant-ui/src/components/Guards
      - ../p2pflow-admin-ui/src
      - ../p2pflow-executor/src/modules/sessions

  errorHandling:
    businessException: typed domain errors mapped to stable HTTP and contract error codes
    codes:
      - INVALID_PRICE_ROUND
      - STALE_PRICE
      - ORDER_STATE_CONFLICT
      - NO_ELIGIBLE_MERCHANT
      - ASSIGNMENT_REJECTED
      - SESSION_INVALID
      - CHAIN_REORG_RETRY
      - TRANSACTION_UNCERTAIN

  diagrams:
    existing:
      - P2PFLOW_MVP_PHASE_1_HIGH_LEVEL.pdf in workspace root
    preferredFormat: mermaid

  repositoryRelationships:
    - primary: p2pflow/p2pflow-smart-contract
      consumes:
        - Circle USDC
    - primary: local/p2pflow-executor
      consumes:
        - p2pflow/p2pflow-smart-contract
        - p2pflow/p2pflow-subgraph
        - PostgreSQL
        - price providers
    - primary: p2pflow/p2pflow-subgraph
      consumes:
        - p2pflow/p2pflow-smart-contract events
    - primary: p2pflow frontends
      consumes:
        - shared ABI/deployment manifest
        - local/p2pflow-executor API
        - p2pflow/p2pflow-subgraph
        - Base Sepolia RPC
```
